D = 6.5e-5 exp(-136000/(8.314×873)).

8.314×873 = 7258.1. 136000/7258.1 = 18.738. exp(-18.738) = ?

exp(-18.738): exp(-18) = 1.523e-8, exp(-0.738)=0.478. So 1.523e-8 × 0.478 = 7.28e-9. Times 6.5e-5 = 4.73e-13.

So D ≈ 4.7e-13 m²/s → J.</think>## Solution

Using the Arrhenius equation for diffusion:

$$D = D_0 \exp\left(-\frac{Q}{RT}\right)$$

**Given values:**
- $D_0 = 6.5 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{m}^2/\text{s}$
- $Q = 136{,}000 \, \text{J/mol}$
- $T = 600°C = 873 \, \text{K}$
- $R = 8.314 \, \text{J/mol·K}$

**Calculation:**

$$\frac{Q}{RT} = \frac{136{,}000}{(8.314)(873)} = \frac{136{,}000}{7258.1} = 18.74$$

$$D = 6.5 \times 10^{-5} \times e^{-18.74}$$

$$D = 6.5 \times 10^{-5} \times 7.28 \times 10^{-9}$$

$$D \approx 4.7 \times 10^{-13} \, \text{m}^2/\text{s}$$

This matches choice J.

Answer: J
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

