Sampling once every 1/8 second → 8 samples per second. 16 states → 4 bits per sample. Rate = 8 × 4 = 32 b/s.</think>**Setting up the problem:**

- The channel samples once every 1/8 second, meaning it takes 8 samples per second (baud rate = 8 baud).
- Each sample can take one of 16 different states.

**Bits per sample:**

With 16 states, each sample carries:
$$\log_2 16 = 4 \text{ bits}$$

**Maximum data rate:**

$$8 \text{ samples/s} \times 4 \text{ bits/sample} = 32 \text{ b/s}$$

