Second reaction: 1-nitropropane + KOH + (E)-but-2-enenitrile + H2O. This is Michael addition of nitroalkane anion to activated alkene (crotononitrile). 1-nitropropane CH3CH2CH2NO2? Deprotonate at carbon bearing nitro (alpha) -> nitronate. Adds to β-carbon of (E)-but-2-enenitrile (crotononitrile CH3-CH=CH-CN? Need numbering but-2-enenitrile: nitrile carbon C1, alkene C2=C3, C4 methyl. (E)-but-2-enenitrile = CH3CH=CHCN, β-carbon is C3 (CH-CH3) or C2? In conjugate addition to α,β-unsaturated nitrile, nucleophile adds to β carbon (C3), protonation at α carbon C2. Product: NC-CH(CH3)-CH(NO2? wait nucleophile attaches at β)?? Let's derive. Crotononitrile CH3-CH=CH-CN (C4-C3=C2-C1 nitrile). β carbon relative CN is C3 (CH-CH3). Nucleophile R (from nitroalkane) adds to C3, proton to C2, giving CH3-CH(R)-CH2-CN? Actually C2 becomes CH2? Starting C2 has H and CN; after protonation C2 gets H -> CH2-CN. C3 has CH3 and R and H? Starting C3 has H and CH3; after addition R replaces pi, C3 has H, CH3, R. Product: NC-CH2-CH(R)-CH3? If R = CH2CH2NO2? Wait nitronate carbon attaches. 1-nitropropane deprotonated at C1: -CH2CH2CH3? Actually 1-nitropropane CH3CH2CH2NO2, alpha carbon is CH2 next to NO2 (terminal). Deprotonation gives nitronate ^-CH2CH2CH3? The carbon bearing NO2 has two H and propyl? Structure CH3CH2CH2NO2: NO2-CH2-CH2-CH3. Deprotonate at NO2-CH2 -> NO2-CH^- -CH2-CH3. Add to β carbon, product after protonation: NO2-CH(CH2CH3)-CH(CH3)-CH2CN? Need combine. Product name choices: B = 3-methyl-4-nitrohexanenitrile or C = 2,3-dimethyl-4-nitrobutanenitrile. Need map.

