- a(1) = 1
- a(n) = n − 1 if n is odd (n ≥ 3)
- a(n) = n + 1 if n is even

The sequence begins: 1, 3, 2, 5, 4, 7, 6, 9, 8, 11, 10, ...

This is an involution (self-inverse), since each swap (n, n+1) applied twice returns the identity.

